course: dictionary
lesson: 961
title: Blowholes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A blowhole is a breathing hole. Whales, dolphins and porpoises have one on the top of the head, and they breathe air through it. «Whales breathe air through a blowhole on top of the head», so a whale must come up to the surface to breathe.
explain: The spray you see from a whale is warm breath, not a fountain of sea water. On a cold day the warm breath can turn into a little cloud, which is why it looks like a blow. Whales are mammals, not fish, so they need air just as you do.
explain: A blowhole can also be a hole in rocks on the coast. When waves come in, sea water is pushed up through it and sprays into the air. The words around the word tell you which kind is meant: a sentence about waves and rocks means the coast kind, not the whale kind.
fact: A blowhole is a hole used for breathing air or letting out spray.
fact: Whales, dolphins and porpoises breathe through a blowhole on the top of the head.
fact: Whales are mammals, not fish, so they must come to the surface to breathe.
fact: Toothed whales have one blowhole, while baleen whales have two.
fact: Coastal blowholes form when waves wear away caves in cliffs; famous ones are in Australia, New Zealand and Hawaii.
exercise: «Whales breathe air through a blowhole on top of the head.» Where is a whale's blowhole? | In the mouth | *On top of the head | Under the fins | On the tail
exercise: The blow from a whale is mostly what? | Smoke from a fire | *Warm breath | Sea water from a fountain | Sand blown up by the wind
exercise: Which kind of blowhole is in rocks? | *A hole on the coast where sea water sprays up when waves come in | A hole in a tree trunk | A hole in the tail of a dolphin | A hole in the top of a whale's head
test: «A whale must come to the surface to breathe through its blowhole.» Why must a whale come up? | To sleep on the rocks | *To breathe air | To eat its food from the seabed | To find a mate
test: How many blowholes does a toothed whale have? | Five | *One | Two | None
exam: «Whales are mammals, not fish: they breathe air through a blowhole.» Which group of animals is a whale in? | *Mammals | Reptiles | Fish | Insects
